- F-245 **Checking symbolic operators for overloading adds 186 errors to the distance in the compiled checker, measured at `d97001d19`, whose code is climb batch 20's gate, with crashes caught per name: 54 clear by known library fixes, and 132 wait on two designs that the curator decides.** As the stage runs, the 186 are 185 errors and three crashes on `||`, in `List`'s api and component and `String`'s component, "E is not in the kind env": a checker crash that no fix or design clears (`perf-probes/symbolic-operators-2/REPORT.md` section 1.3). The check was turned on in a copy of the checker whose three loops admit every operator; the checker as built skips them (row 584). PLAN, "Pavol's answers", item 59 brings the two designs to the curator: a bound on the subscripts' index type (124 errors), and a vector plus a number beside a vector plus a vector (8). The probe's candidates S1, an index bound with a rule for tuple indices, and A2, `Vector` and `Matrix` leaving `AdditiveGroup`, clear them with nothing new; A3, the scalar `+` and `-` dropped, also clears the 8. The largest families are the subscripts over a generic `Indexed` (124) and `String`'s four concatenation operators, `||`, `|||`, `//` and `///` (40). An earlier measurement, at `d212b2c1f`, counted 205; batches since cleared `FlatString`'s pair (2; F-259) and 20 of the 21 `^` errors (F-263), and added 3: `|_|` 1 and the scalar `+` and `-` 2. Walk's meet check, which also skips symbolic operators and judges neither `String`'s pairs, the subscripts, `^` nor `=`, refused only `EmptyString`'s `||` when widened the same way in the first probe of these operators. Detail: `perf-probes/symbolic-operators-2/REPORT.md` sections 0 to 2; `perf-probes/symbolic-operators/REPORT.md` section 1.5.
